weightsmith
=======

Method
- This project replicates the protocol of: Takehi et al., "Weight-Space Programming",
  MIT, November 2026. https://rikiyat.github.io/blog/weight-space-programming/
  No code from that work is included.

Vendored code
- weightsmith/lab/{openpi_probe,openpi_vlm_full,openpi_head,sandbox}.py are vendored, trimmed copies
  of src/weight_space_policy_lab/ from the authors' earlier project "weight-space-policy-lab"
  (same authors, released here under this repository's MIT license). Only the functions this
  harness uses were kept; their logic is unchanged.
- weightsmith/run_batched.py is derived from RoboLab's Pi0-family evaluation script
  (Copyright (c) 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES, Apache-2.0; header retained). It is
  modified to use the batched, seeded client in weightsmith/batched_client.py.

Separate dependencies (not included; each under its own license)
- OpenPI (Physical Intelligence), including the pi05_droid_jointpos checkpoint, used through a
  fork that supports request-scoped sampling seeds.
- RoboLab and NVIDIA Isaac Sim / Isaac Lab.
- Claude Code (Anthropic) and the OpenAI Codex CLI, used as editor front-ends.

third_party/patches/ contains patch files against two Apache-2.0 projects, applied by scripts/setup_deps.sh:
  - OpenPI (Physical Intelligence; fork github.com/xuningy/openpi @ aa64205): request-scoped sampling seeds.
  - RoboLab (NVIDIA, github.com/NVlabs/RoboLab @ 0aef241 = v0.2.1): seeded/batched policy clients, environment
    seeds, matched steering tasks, predicate-oracle prompt control, task-discovery fix.
envs/robolab-sim/ pins the Isaac Sim 5.0 / Isaac Lab 2.2 environment used for all reported results.
